      "id": 58079,
      "name": "Koey",
      "username": "Koey",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/koey/{size}/2187_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-04-06T23:13:18.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Multani1141\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/50afbb/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Multani1141:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Picked up the enhanced edition and have been playing two player games. We have lost all seven games we have played so far. This game seems tough! Our first game was Omnitron against Haka and Absolute Zero.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I would suggest playing at least 2 Heroes each. As the game is designed with 3-5 Heros but can be played 2-5. Its not widely advertised but Page 11 does say if you are playing with 2 players its advised to play with 2 each.</p>\n<p>Though even then the game is tough <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
      "post_number": 2,
